I got a great bones file today with my latest Tourist.  It was
minetown... as soon as I walked into town I knew something was wrong.
My large beastly dog (72hps) stupidly tried to kill the guard captain
and a guard at the same time as a rock troll was in sight.  I fell back
and burned Elbereth with a lightning wand and prayed for the best.  The
poor thing got himself killed but I had a scroll of taming so I tamed
the troll, and pretty soon the whole guard was dead.

That's just the beginning.  As I got into town I spotted a yellow
dragon (and I'm lvl 4!) in the temple. I was lucky to find a shield of
reflection (indeed it was my only armor except a pair of iron boots) in
a store on DLVL2, so it couldn't touch me from a distance.  Some dwarf
had picked up a wand of fire -- from a bonespile it turns out -- and
delivered it to me, so I somehow took out the dragon by emptying my
wands of lightning and fire, plus throwing all my darts and daggers,
while standing on a permanently-Elberethed square.

I found not one, not two, but five (5) bones piles.  A samurai named
Jack, a character of unknown class named Theophilus, another samurai,
another tourist, and a possible wizard.  Oh, and the minetown priest
was dead.  And some shopkeepers were dead.

It was a painstaking process carrying all their loot to the altar to
b/u/c and identify it. I made an enormous stack of stuff that I thought
was safe because of all the curses ... it hadn't occured to me that
monsters would use it.  I didn't think monsters used polymorph wands
either, of which there were at least three in the stash.

Well along came an uruk-hai who put on the yellow dragon scales and
zapped himself with a cursed poly wand -- OMG another yellow dragon!

I consider myself SO lucky I was able to get back upstairs with my
troll.

Now I'm level 8 and have one new wand of lightning, plus much better
armor (-8AC) and some throwing daggers.  Think I've got a chance?



